{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You shall not kindle fire.</b> Rashi explained: some of our Sages say — the kindling came out as a negative prohibition, etc. That is, the kindling that went out from the general category of 'you shall not do any work' on Shabbat went out as a negative prohibition to remove it from the stringency of the other labors, and to teach about it that it is liable to neither extirpation nor death but only to a negative prohibition — these are the words of Rabbi Yosei; Rabbi Natan says: it went out to distinguish. That is, to tell you: just as this one is singled out, for it is among the principal labors done in the Tabernacle, and the verse held it liable on its own account in [the matter of] the Tabernacle, for it singled it out alone, so too anything that is a principal labor — if one did many of them in one lapse of awareness, he is liable for each and every one. And anything that was in a general category and went out from the general category — it went out not to teach about itself, but to teach about the entire general category. Thus Rashi explained in general. <b>You shall not kindle fire.</b> According to its plain sense, it warned about kindling more than about the other labors, because it does not appear to be a labor; but one prepares everything on the eve of Shabbat, and kindles the coals on Shabbat in order to work with gold and silver and copper immediately after Shabbat. Another interpretation: lest they say — behold, above, in the pericope of Bo, he forbade us on a festival all labor of service, but permitted labor for food; so too on Shabbat, labor for food should be permitted. Therefore it says <b>you shall not kindle fire</b> — even for baking and cooking, for fire is a requirement for all food." "<b>In all your dwellings.</b> But in the Temple it is permitted to do."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "The comment cites Rashi by the abbreviation פירש״י, resolved here as 'Rashi explained.' The phrase וכו' (etc.) is rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:04.725492938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}